+# Round 7 T-dense report
+
+Status: IN PROGRESS. All edits are confined to this report and tdense7_scratch. No commits or subagents. Mathematical computation is restricted to DIRICHLET_IP=34.148.157.169 src/dirun.sh -c 2. Optimization uses Gurobi, Threads=2, NonConvex=2 when needed.
+
+PROVED target definition (quoted). T-dense(C) means: there exists c(C)>0 such that every finite nonempty set A of distinct positive integers, with X=max A<=C n and n=|A|, satisfies M(A)>=c(C)sqrt(n), where f_A(x)=sum cos(ax) and M(A)=-min over all real x.
+
+PROVED source audit. Read CLAUDE.md; P29, P31, P31-C, P36, P38, P44, P47, P49, P53; NOTEBOOK night continuation 6; E70/E70b/E72/E72c; the exact high-pass implementation e70_p47_scan.py and the annealer e72_p47_pareto.c. P31 and the stable-Gram argument are quoted ingredients. No claim of external priority is made.
+
+HEURISTIC frontier and three active lines. (1) Replace P47's model/discrepancy selection by a diagonal exact high-pass argument for arbitrary binary sequences. (2) Combine the resulting profile constraints with a quantitative positive-definite profile energy gap. (3) Optimize the profile escape constraints and realize the escaping profiles as genuine sets. The first two concern universal lower bounds; the third tests the putative construction mechanism.
+
+## Initial proof candidate, undergoing adversarial audit
+
+CONJECTURED at this checkpoint. T-dense(3) follows by compactness, with no effective constant yet, from the following calculation. For a hypothetical sequence M=o(sqrt(X)), take a weak macroscopic density p on [0,1], integral d>=1/3. The even zero extension is continuous positive definite (P48); put a=p(0), b=integral p(1-p), and r=0.8110 (P31-E). P31 and a diagonal exact high-pass should give a>=2d/r and a(1-a)>=2b/r.
+
+PROVED auxiliary inequality, paper derivation. For any continuous positive-definite even p supported in [-1,1], with 0<=p<=a=p(0)<=1 and d=integral_0^1 p, the spectral triangle inequality gives p(t)<=a(1-t^2/4). Indeed N=floor(1/t)+1 has Nt>1 and N<=2/t, and a-p(Nt)<=N^2(a-p(t)). Thus integral p^2<=a d-d^3/(12a), by integral t^2 p>=d^3/(3a^2). Consequently b>=d(1-a)+d^3/(12a). This is the quoted stable-Gram mechanism applied after normalizing the identity value to a; the combination with P31/P47 is new relative to this record.
+
+CONJECTURED remaining algebraic check. The preceding bounds force
+
+    a(1-a)(a-2d/r) >= d^3/(6r).
+
+At d=1/3 and r=0.8110 this appears impossible, with a small strict margin. The VM will check the extremal cubic and independent exact rational bounds. The proof still needs the full diagonal high-pass argument and the compactness quantifiers; no theorem is declared from this sketch.
+
+NUMERICAL experiments pending. The first VM call checks tool availability. Planned falsification: adapt the existing annealer, fixing the box endpoint at 3n and minimizing the best P31/P47 bound plus a small M penalty; then independently reevaluate the saved sets. Planned profile computation: Gurobi nonconvex quadratic constraints for p_i(1-p_i), all sampled window scales, explicitly distinguishing fixed-origin profiles from alternate-model and PD constraints.
