13:## R7-T: T-dense(3), full compactness proof
84:## Strategic review after the first two attacks
86:PROVED advance. Model selection is unnecessary for an ineffective theorem: exact high-pass multiplication plus a diagonal strong-L2 smoothing limit supplies P47's energy conditions for arbitrary sets. The normalized identity value a in the stable-Gram inequality is essential; replacing it by 1 loses the C=3 contradiction. Both parts have been derived with all sequence quantifiers above.
92:## R7-CF: T-dense(4.331), with exact rational certificate
120:PROVED finite exact certificate, executable verification on the VM. envelope_exact.py checks every segment minimum using Fraction arithmetic. It reports a strict positive margin for C=4.164 at r=.811, and C=4.331 at r=.77. These finite inequalities combined with R7-T's compactness steps prove T-dense(4.164) using P31-E alone, and T-dense(4.331) using quoted P31-N, since 4/(3sqrt(3))<.77. Both constants c(C) remain ineffective. The exact certificate is in envelope_exact.json. The decimal locations from envelope.py (4.164686 at .811 and 4.332215 at the Beckner limit) are NUMERICAL diagnostics of this particular scalar envelope, not the reach of all windows or all models.
